<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place</p><h1 class="enc-title">First Cataract</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The First Cataract is the stretch of rapids and granite islands on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nile">Nile</a> at Aswan, the northernmost of the river's cataracts. For much of antiquity it marked the southern frontier of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nubia">Nubia</a>, and its quarries supplied granite for monuments. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/senusret-iii">Senusret III</a> had a canal cut through it for boats, and the Aswan dams of the twentieth century were built at and above it.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/first-cataract.jpg" alt="First Cataract" width="320" height="669" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: The original uploader was Mark Dingemanse at English Wikipedia. · CC BY 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nubia_today.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
